create-network-tshoot-livecd (1.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix Ubuntu builds end-to-end (two more Debian-live-build-on-Ubuntu quirks):
    - Kernel meta-package: set --linux-flavours per base (generic for Ubuntu,
      amd64 for Debian); Debian's live-build kept linux-image-amd64 in ubuntu
      mode, failing with "no installation candidate".
    - apt Signed-By conflict: wire the OBS repo via live-build's archives
      mechanism for both stages (.chroot + .binary) with one consistent
      no-signed-by trust config, instead of a second includes.chroot source with
      signed-by (which Ubuntu's apt rejects). The source now persists into the
      image on every base.

 -- Ciro Iriarte <ciro.iriarte+software@gmail.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 00:19:46 -0500

create-network-tshoot-livecd (1.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix Ubuntu builds: pass the apt mirror explicitly. Debian's live-build
    leaves every mirror variable empty for --mode ubuntu, producing a malformed
    sources.list ("deb  jammy main universe" with no URL) that aborts the chroot
    stage. Set --mirror-* and --parent-mirror-* (archive + security) for every
    base; add --mirror URL to override with an internal mirror when air-gapped.

 -- Ciro Iriarte <ciro.iriarte+software@gmail.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 23:41:50 -0500

create-network-tshoot-livecd (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bootloader serial console: the GRUB (UEFI) and isolinux (BIOS) boot menus
    are now mirrored to the serial console, not just VGA. Previously only the
    kernel and getty reached serial; the boot menu was VGA-only.
  * Add --serial-unit N (default 0) selecting the ttyS<N> unit used by BOTH the
    kernel console and the bootloader menu (the bootloader cannot auto-discover
    the port). The kernel cmdline now uses the selected unit instead of a fixed
    ttyS0+ttyS1 pair; runtime login auto-discovery on other UARTs is unchanged.
  * Honor http_proxy/https_proxy for build hosts without direct Internet: curl
    (OBS key) and debootstrap read them from the environment, and the in-chroot
    apt is forwarded the value via --apt-http-proxy. Run under `sudo -E` so the
    proxy reaches root's environment. Unrelated to --proxy, which configures the
    booted diagnostic system's runtime network.

 -- Ciro Iriarte <ciro.iriarte+software@gmail.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 21:38:03 -0500

create-network-tshoot-livecd (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. Distro-independent, boot-only cabling-diagnostics LiveCD
    builder (a live-build wrapper). Boots a target host into a RAM-resident
    environment, identifies it from a CSV persona inventory (DMI serial ->
    hostname, optional bonded-VLAN management IP), brings up every physical
    NIC, runs nic-xray + lldpd, and prints a per-NIC cabling report to VGA and
    an auto-discovered serial console, then drops to a root shell. Writes
    nothing to local disks.
  * Relocated from the pve-tools repository (was pve-create-tshoot-livecd);
    dropped the Proxmox naming and the sibling ReaR restore tool.

 -- Ciro Iriarte <ciro.iriarte+software@gmail.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 19:51:07 -0500
